+## Splitting a big DOL unit's claim around one function
+
+Measured 2026-09-26 in lane `cgo`, on `CGameGlobalObjects`'s constructor. The recipe is worth
+having because the same shape recurs - a 228-byte function inside a 17,608-byte `NonMatching`
+claim, worth exactly one `Matching` unit and one `linked` function, is the shape every remaining
+boot-path function has.
+
+**What it took.** `main.cpp` claimed one contiguous `.text` range, 0x800053B8-0x80009880. The
+constructor is 0x8000848C-0x80008570, inside it. Three things had to move, and two of them are
+not in `configure.py`:
+
+1. **`config/G2ME01/splits.txt`, three units instead of one.** `main.cpp` 0x800053B8-0x8000848C,
+   `MetroidPrime/CGameGlobalObjectsCtor.cpp` 0x8000848C-0x80008570 (`Matching`),
+   `MetroidPrime/mainTail.cpp` 0x80008570-0x80009880 plus **`.ctors` 0x803A54A4 and `.sbss`
+   0x80418EA0**.
+2. **The source moved with the ranges, into `mainTail.cpp`** - `sMainSpace`, `__sys_free`,
+   `CMain::CMain`, `InvokeCMain`, `~CMain`, `SetGameFrameDrawn`, `fn_80008A1C`, `SetMaxSpeed`,
+   `InitializeSubsystems`, `ShutdownSubsystems`, `~CPlayerState`, `~SPersistentState`,
+   `~CStaticInterference`, `~CGameArchitectureSupport` and the four weak template copies they
+   drag in. *objdiff pairs a unit's functions by name against **that** unit's retail list*, and
+   fifteen of those were at 100% in `main/MetroidPrime/main`; leaving their bodies in `main.cpp`
+   trades fifteen off the `matched` total to gain one.
+3. **`config/G2ME01/symbols.txt`, two renames**: `fn_802FB154` -> `__ct__11CResFactoryFv` and
+   `fn_80301008` -> `__ct__11CSimplePoolFR8IFactory`.
+
+**Why the cut cannot be anywhere else, which is the part that is not a choice.** `dtk dol split`
+walks the configured units in order and requires each one's claimed addresses to be
+non-decreasing; `main.cpp` calls the constructor, so it must come first; the constructor's range
+is therefore the middle one and everything above it is a single range starting at 0x80008570.
+`.ctors` and `.sbss` have to be on the **last** unit in the list, because with them on `main.cpp`
+dtk fails with `Mismatched splits for .ctors 4:0x803A54A4 (MetroidPrime/main.cpp) and function
+3:0x80009864 (MetroidPrime/mainTail.cpp)`. A cut at 0x80007A14 instead - putting
+`CGameArchitectureSupport`'s constructor and destructor here as well, which is what recovers
+`ReleaseData__rc_ptr<CIOWin>`, `__dt__rstl::list<CArchitectureMessage>` and
+`__dl__TOneStatic<CGameArchitectureSupport>` without a trick - puts the constructor's range
+*inside* the tail unit's, and that is a two-range unit again.
+
+**Three negative results, all measured, none of them obvious:**
+
+* **A DOL unit may not claim two ranges in the same section.** `splits.txt` accepts a repeated
+  entry (`Runtime/__init_cpp_exceptions.cpp` has two `.dtors`), and it is the obvious way to keep
+  `main.cpp` whole, but `dtk` then fails with `Cyclic dependency encountered while resolving link
+  order: MetroidPrime/main.cpp -> MetroidPrime/CGameGlobalObjectsCtor.cpp` - `main.cpp` calls the
+  constructor, and the constructor stores into `main.cpp`'s `.sbss`. The REL-module three-way
+  prefix/matching/tail splits work because a REL unit is not in a link order with its
+  neighbours. A *definition* on both sides does it too: a new unit that defines
+  `gpCharacterFactoryBuilder` while `main.cpp` still claims the `.sbss` range holding it produces
+  the same message, and the fix is to `extern` it.
+* **A class's member constructor is only spelled three ways, and only one of them is retail's.**
+  `CResFactory` and `CSimplePool` both have a virtual base, so an inline constructor body makes
+  mwcceppc emit the base-class vptr store (and, for `CSimplePool`, the whole `rstl::hash_map`
+  default construction) **in the caller**: 36 instructions where retail's caller has two. A
+  declared-only constructor emits the call and nothing else - and then the call is
+  `__ct__11CResFactoryFv`, which the DOL does not define under that name, so the two renames are
+  forced. For a class with **no** base the inline-body form is right and needs no rename
+  (`CGameGlobalObjectsCardInit` -> `fn_803096C4`, `CCharacterFactoryBuilder` -> `fn_80032008`,
+  `CGameGlobalObjectsTail` -> `fn_801F0A44`).
+* **A weak COMDAT copy is not a blocker.** `unit_fit.sh` lists five extra functions and 476 bytes
+  in this unit - `__dt__Q24rstl22single_ptr<9IRenderer>Fv` and four siblings, which mwcceppc emits
+  because `CGameGlobalObjects` has four `single_ptr`s and an `optional_object` and it
+  instantiates a class template's members eagerly. **Declaring `~CGameGlobalObjects()` does not
+  stop it.** `flip_test.sh` PASSes anyway, on the CAi precedent: mwldeppc discards the duplicates
+  and the DOL comes out retail's bytes. Read the note under `unit_fit.sh`'s "extra" list before
+  spending a session on it.
+
+**Two source-writing details that decided the last two instructions,** both of which are the
+"named temporary" lever from "One instruction of register allocation" above: `return self != 0 ?
+fn_801449C8(self) : self;` gives `stw r3,304(r31)` where retail has `mr r0,r3 ; stw r0,304(r31)`,
+and so do an extra `static_cast` and a `reinterpret_cast<unsigned int>` round trip. Only
+`CGameState* made = self; if (made != 0) { made = f(made); } return made;` fixes it, and it fixes
+both allocations at once. And retail's file operand for a `new` here is **`lbl_803A56C0`**, not
+the `lbl_803A9208` that `CGameStateCtor.cpp` names - one merged `.rodata` pool per blob, and
+`lbl_803A56C0` is where the pak names and `"%d"` live.
+
+**And the port side, which is a separate problem and a separate number.** The constructor is the
+whole of retail boot step 7 and it is now byte-exact, but **listing it in `files.cmake` makes the
+port's link worse: 325 -> 333 undefined, 0 closed.** Two of the eight are `CSimplePool`'s
+constructor and destructor, three are retail functions with no host body at all
+(`fn_803096C4`, `fn_80032008`, `fn_801F0A44`, `fn_8016C230`), one is `fn_801449C8` (excluded from
+the port build for the same reason) and one is `lbl_80418EC8`. The port needs a *caller* -
+`CMain::RsMain` in `PortBoot.cpp` is host-only and checks `gpGameState` for null rather than
+constructing the object that fills it - and bodies for those six, in that order. Write it down
+rather than inferring it from "the unit is Matching".
+
